diagonalMultidegrees -- t-tuples of non-negative integers with sum equal to d
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        diagonalMultidegrees(d,t)
        diagonalMultidegrees(d,L)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the (non-negative) sum of the
        tuples
      * t, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the length of the tuples
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the maximum value for each
        coordinate
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing lists of t integers each

Description
===========

Given numbers d and t, this function gives all lists of t non-negative integers
where the sum of each list is equal to d. If the second input is a list L, the
tuples have the same length as L and are constrained to have i-th entry at most
1+L_i.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : t = 2                                           |
|                                                     |
|o1 = 2                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : d = 5                                           |
|                                                     |
|o2 = 5                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : diagonalMultidegrees(d,t)                       |
|                                                     |
|o3 = {{0, 5}, {1, 4}, {2, 3}, {3, 2}, {4, 1}, {5, 0}}|
|                                                     |
|o3 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : diagonalMultidegrees(d, {0,1,2})                |
|                                                     |
|o4 = {{0, 2, 3}, {1, 1, 3}, {1, 2, 2}}               |
|                                                     |
|o4 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

