findMins -- calculates the minimal elements of a subset of ZZ^r
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        findMins L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, subset of $\ZZ^r$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, minimal elements

Description
===========

Given a list L of elements in $\ZZ^r$, this function will return the minimal
elements of L under the partial order where $c\leq d$ if and only if $c_i\leq
d_i$ for all $1\leq i\leq r$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = {{1,2},{3,1},{3,2},{1,4}}   |
|                                     |
|o1 = {{1, 2}, {3, 1}, {3, 2}, {1, 4}}|
|                                     |
|o1 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : findMins L                      |
|                                     |
|o2 = {{1, 2}, {3, 1}}                |
|                                     |
|o2 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+

The algorithm constructs a monomial ideal by using the elements of the list as
exponents.  Such an ideal can also be given directly.

See also
========

  * *note findRegion: findRegion, -- finds minimal multidegree(s) in a given
    region where an ideal or module satisfies a Boolean function

