linearTruncations -- finds minimal multidegree(s) in a given range where the resolution of a truncated module is linear
***********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        linearTruncations(L,M)
        linearTruncations M
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing 2 lists: minimum and
        maximum multidegrees defining range
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the module to be truncated
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing multidegrees with linear
        truncations

Description
===========

Given a list {L1,L2} and a module $M$, this function truncates $M$ at each
multidegree between L1 and L2 and tests whether the minimal resolution of the
resulting module is linear.  The set of multidegrees producing linear
resolutions is invariant under positive translation, and the function returns
the minimal multidegrees in this set.  If a list L is not provided it will
search between the componentwise minimum of the degrees of the generators of
$M$ and the degree with all coordinates equal to $r+1$, where $r$ is the *note
regularity: (Macaulay2Doc)regularity, of $M$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = multigradedPolynomialRing({2,3},Standard=>false)                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker map(S^{{0,-3},{0,-3},{-3,0},{-3,0},{-3,0},{-3,0}},S^{{-3,-3   |
|     {{a^3,b^3,c^3, 0,0,0},{0,0,0,b^3,a^3,c^3},{-d^3,0,0,-d^3,0,0},{0,-e^3   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = cokernel {0, 3} | a3  b3  c3  0   0   0   |                             |
|              {0, 3} | 0   0   0   b3  a3  c3  |                             |
|              {3, 0} | -d3 0   0   -d3 0   0   |                             |
|              {3, 0} | 0   -e3 0   0   -e3 0   |                             |
|              {3, 0} | 0   0   -f3 0   0   -f3 |                             |
|              {3, 0} | 0   0   0   -g3 0   0   |                             |
|                                                                             |
|                             6                                               |
|o2 : S-module, quotient of S                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|},{-3,-3},{-3,-3},{-3,-3},{-3,-3},{-3,-3}},                                  |
|,0,0,-e^3,0},{0,0,-f^3,0,0,-f^3},{0,0,0,-g^3,0,0}})                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : linearTruncations M                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{3, 3}}                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : linearTruncations({{0,0},{9,9}}, M)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{3, 3}, {8, 2}}                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

With the default options there may be generators of the linear truncation
region not contained in the search region and thus not returned.

See also
========

  * *note coarseMultigradedRegularity:
    (TateOnProducts)coarseMultigradedRegularity, -- A truncation that has
    linear resolution
  * *note isLinearComplex: isLinearComplex, -- tests whether a complex of
    graded modules is linear

Ways to use linearTruncations:
==============================

  * "linearTruncations(List,Module)"
  * "linearTruncations(Module)"

