regularityBound -- bounds the multigraded regularity of a module
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        regularityBound M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a multigraded module with no
        $H^0_B$ or $H^1_B$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing multidegrees in the
        regularity of M

Description
===========

Using only the multigraded betti numbers of a $\ZZ^r$-graded module $M$, this
function identifies a subset of the multigraded regularity of a module $M$ over
the coordinate ring $S$ of a product of projective spaces, in the sense of
Maclagan and Smith.  It assumes that the local cohomology groups $H^0_B(M)$ and
$H^1_B(M)$ vanish, where $B$ is the irrelevant ideal of $S$.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : (S,E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces {1,2}|
|                                            |
|o1 = (S, E)                                 |
|                                            |
|o1 : Sequence                               |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x_(0,0)*x_(1,0),x_(1,1)^3)   |
|                                            |
|                       3                    |
|o2 = ideal (x   x   , x   )                 |
|             0,0 1,0   1,1                  |
|                                            |
|o2 : Ideal of S                             |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = S^1/I                              |
|                                            |
|o3 = cokernel | x_(0,0)x_(1,0) x_(1,1)^3 |  |
|                                            |
|                            1               |
|o3 : S-module, quotient of S                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : regularityBound M                      |
|                                            |
|o4 = {{0, 2}}                               |
|                                            |
|o4 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : needsPackage "VirtualResolutions"      |
|                                            |
|o5 = VirtualResolutions                     |
|                                            |
|o5 : Package                                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : multigradedRegularity(S,M)             |
|                                            |
|o6 = {{0, 2}}                               |
|                                            |
|o6 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

The output is often but not always {partialRegularities M}.

Caveat
======

In general regularityBound will not give the minimal elements of
$\operatorname{reg} M$ but will be faster than computing cohomology.

See also
========

  * *note partialRegularities: partialRegularities, -- calculates
    Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity in each component of a multigrading
  * *note isQuasiLinear: isQuasiLinear, -- checks whether degrees in the
    resolution of a truncation are at most those of the irrelevant ideal
  * *note multigradedRegularity: (VirtualResolutions)multigradedRegularity, --
    computes the minimal elements of the multigraded regularity of a module
    over a multigraded ring

Ways to use regularityBound:
============================

  * "regularityBound(Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note regularityBound: regularityBound, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

